# Simulator-regenerable datasets are provisioned on demand by the consuming
# scripts' `should_simulate()` bootstrap (see any scripts/*/*.py) — they must
# NOT be committed. Everything under dataset/ is ignored; only real/external
# data (observational or hand-authored truth-model inputs the simulators read,
# not produce) is re-included via the `!` allowlist below. The dataset-allowlist
# guard (PyAutoHands check_dataset_allowlist.py) enforces this.
dataset/**
!dataset/.gitignore
!dataset/cluster/**
!dataset/interferometer/uv_wavelengths/**
!dataset/point_source/simple/**
